.TH XUR.STD.NUM 7 "2026-10-27" "xur 0.1.1" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.num \- integer and float methods
.SH DESCRIPTION
These are methods on integer and float values, available directly without
importing a module.
.SS Integer methods (i64)
.TP
.B abs() -> i64
Absolute value.
.TP
.B pow(exp: u32) -> i64
Raise to the power
.IR exp .
.TP
.B min(other) -> i64
The smaller of the two.
.TP
.B max(other) -> i64
The larger of the two.
.TP
.B to_float() -> f64
Convert to a float.
.TP
.B to_string() -> str
Decimal string representation.
.TP
.B to_hex() -> str
Lowercase hexadecimal string representation.
.SS Float methods (f64)
.TP
.B abs() -> f64
Absolute value.
.TP
.B sqrt() -> f64
Square root.
.TP
.B floor() -> f64
Round toward negative infinity.
.TP
.B ceil() -> f64
Round toward positive infinity.
.TP
.B round() -> f64
Round to the nearest integer (half away from zero).
.TP
.B to_int() -> i64
Truncate to an integer.
.TP
.B to_string() -> str
String representation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::io;

fn main() {
    io::println("{}", (-5).abs());
    io::println("{}", 255.to_hex());
    io::println("{}", 3.14.floor());
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std (7),
.BR xur.std.math (7)
